      "report_location": {
        "agent_output_id": "12591384-0b26-470d-a99d-a49c00be440b:aggressive_risk_analyst:risk_debate_state.aggressive_history",
        "char_offset": 459,
        "claim_index": 4,
        "paragraph": "First, to the conservative analyst: your entire thesis rests on the receivables and FCF deterioration, and I'm going to dismantle that. You're pointing at AR growing +54.9% QoQ against revenue +17.9% QoQ and calling it a red flag. But look at what's actually happening underneath. This is a company that just grew revenue 106% year-over-year, from $46.7B to $96.2B in four quarters. When you're onboarding hyperscaler customers at that velocity — and the report explicitly notes these are large hyperscaler customers being extended terms — receivables balloon because the customer base is transforming from a broad retail/enterprise mix into a handful of mega-cap buyers who negotiate 60-90 day terms",
        "section": null
      },
      "text": "This is a company that just grew revenue 106% year-over-year, from $46.7B to $96.2B in four quarters."
    },
